================================================================================
                   COMMAND CHAINING: Pipes & Logic
================================================================================

COMMAND                          PURPOSE
--------                         --------
cmd1 | cmd2                      Pipe: output of cmd1 feeds into cmd2
cmd1 && cmd2                     Run cmd2 only if cmd1 succeeds
cmd1 ; cmd2                      Run both commands in sequence
cmd1 || cmd2                     Run cmd2 only if cmd1 FAILS

EXAMPLES:
    cat scroll | grep "rift"     Search this scroll for "rift"
    ls -la && echo "Success"     List files, then print success
    ls | wc -l                   Count items in a room

